              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "LOOKING AT CELLS AND MOLECULES IN THE ELECTRON MICROSCOPE 588  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Electron Microscope Resolves the Fine Structure of the Cell 588  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Biological Specimens Require Special Preparation for Electron Microscopy 589  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Heavy Metals Can Provide Additional Contrast 590  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Images of Surfaces Can Be Obtained by Scanning Electron Microscopy 591  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Electron Microscope Tomography Allows the Molecular Architecture of Cells to Be Seen in Three Dimensions 593  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Cryo-electron Microscopy Can Determine Molecular Structures at Atomic Resolution 595  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Light Microscopy and Electron Microscopy Are Mutually Beneficial 597  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Using Microscopy to Study Cells Always Involves Trade-Offs 598  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 599  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Problems 600  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "References 601"
                }
              ]
            }
